#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# digamma

#% text
# `digamma(x)` gives the digamma function, the derivative of `log(gamma(x))`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `digamma(x)` is `gamma'(x)/gamma(x)` (DLMF 5.2.2). It has simple poles at 0, -1, -2, ...

#% item
# Positive integers and half-integers give exact values in terms of `euler_gamma`, `log(2)` and harmonic numbers; machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# `digamma` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
digamma(1)
#% output
#= -euler_gamma

#% cell
digamma(4)
#% output
#= 11/6 - euler_gamma

#% cell
digamma(1/2)
#% output
#= -2*log(2) - euler_gamma

#% cell
digamma(2.5)
#% output
#= 0.7031566406452432

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# 30 digits:

#% cell
n(digamma(1/3), 30)
#% output
#= -3.132033780020806322996419074287269

#% text
# A complex argument:

#% cell
digamma(1.0 + 1.0*im)
#% output
#= 0.09465032062247669 + 1.076674047468581im

#% text
# A negative argument between the poles:

#% cell
digamma(-0.5)
#% output
#= 0.03648997397857652

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The recurrence `digamma(x + 1) = digamma(x) + 1/x`:

#% cell
digamma(3.7) - digamma(2.7) - 1/2.7
#% output
#= 0.0

#% text
# The derivative is `polygamma(1, x)`:

#% cell
d(digamma(x), x)
#% output
#= polygamma(1, x)

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# The poles have no value:

#% cell
digamma(0)
#% output
#! failure(pole, digamma(0))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `polygamma`, `log_gamma`, `gamma`, `harmonic_number`, `euler_gamma`
